    "summary": "A skirt cloth, possibly an &#039;ulos runjat&#039;.  Rectangular; cream and blue/black (indigo dyed) warp ikat stripes on a mid-brown &#039;ground&#039;; warp faced tabby cloth; solid blue/black stripe at sides.  Made of three separate sections hand sewn edge along selvedges: central panel 60 cms wide; two side panels 26 cms each.  Thin line of plain red rows of twining (&#039;hotang-hotang&#039;) beside thin plied fringes. There is also supplementary warp decoration.",
